spans.s:
cl. 1. च॑तति, ‘to hide one's self’. See च॑तत् and च॑त्त;
to go, Naigh. ii, 14;
 P. and Ā. to ask, beg (= √ चद्), Dhātup. xxi, 5 :
Caus. चात॑यति, ˚ते (aor. अचीचत्तम्, अचीचते, TĀr. ii, 4, 5 f.), ‘to cause to hide’, scare, frighten away, RV. iv, 17, 9; x, 155, 1; AV. iv, xix (cf. निश्-, प्र-, वि-; cf. also चातक, चातन, चात्त्र.)
